the first anniversary of the deadly  january 6th assault on the capitol  former president trump has cancelled a  rally scheduled to mark the occasion in  his way tomorrow  and the house select committee  investigating the attack meanwhile is  seeking cooperation from fox news host  sean hannity about his communication  with the white house before the riot the  committee has also expressed interest in  speaking directly with former vice  president mike pence  meanwhile tomorrow's anniversary may be  a struggle for some of the police  officers who were beaten and abused by  rioters on that day  senior investigative correspondent  catherine herridge sat down with a  veteran capitol police officer who is  demanding accountability catherine good  morning tony sergeant angelina gunnell  told cbs news that january 6 was the day  he thought he would die  at the west entrance as rioter scaled  scaffolding set up for the inauguration  capitol police sergeant akolina gonnell  was beaten and his spirit nearly broken  are you suffering yes i mean  from  every  day for me it's been a january 6. on  twitter the 16-year veteran of the  capitol police force documented his  injuries to dispel claims that minimize  last year's violence canal told us he  still can't shake the trauma the way i  sleep  from that way  by  the way i put my shirt on the way i take  a shower  the physical therapy twice a week  the mental health therapy  once a week gannel who testified to  congress earlier this year is now doing  administrative work rather than patrols  it's been hard emotionally physically  and financially as well too the select  committee investigating the attack on  the capitol now wants to hear from fox  news host sean hannity about his text  messages with the white house before the  riots on december 31st hannity texted  then white house chief of staff mark  meadows i do not see january 6 happening  the way he is being told five days later  to an unknown recipient hannity wrote  i'm very worried about the next 48 hours  and on january 10th to meadows and ohio  congressman jim jordan guys we have a  clear path to land the plane in nine  days he can't mention the election again  hannity's lawyer told cbs news they are  reviewing the committee's request  now nearly a year after about 140 police  officers were assaulted some with lethal  weapons gunnell says action needs to be  taken to prevent this from happening  again if  we don't put a deterrent on some of  these  and hold people accountable for what  they did  this could be a recurring  thing every four years  three more officers who defended the  capitol on january 6 are suing former  president trump for his alleged wrongful  conduct inciting a riot this lawsuit  should be heard by a federal judge next  week tony  concept of that happening every four  years is chilling catherine thank you  very much for that interview
 

